{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 43 (chapter 4, The Wild Heart): four tribes on one round continent, all hostile. The player lives in the south; the western war tribe (tribe 1, aggressive), the northern stone keepers (tribe 2, turtle) and the eastern raiders (tribe 3, sneaky) each live on a mesa walled by cliffs (disc aboveSea 104, falloff 2), so no army climbs one until its stage, when six shape steps raise a ramp on the face toward the center. Every rival is capped (maxPopulation 24, 24 and 22, maxTroops 8) and keeps posted guards and towers. A crown of three stones (ley, ward, seer) on the central hill is held by the stone keepers, dormant until the raiders fall, with 6 posted wardens and 2 firecallers. Stages: grow to 34 followers (an idle village falls to 5 raiders landing on the southeast shore every 150 s from 420 s, until 0); kill 12 eastern raiders (4 wardens and a firecaller from below the east mesa and 4 wardens from the southeast shore every 90 s, until 1); burn the raiders' Hearth (east ramp; 10 wardens, 3 firecallers, 2 towers, 3 more wardens every 75 s); hold two crown stones at once for 180 s (the stone keepers and the war tribe each send 4 wardens to pray them back every 120 s, until 3); kill 12 of the war tribe (bands of 6 and 4 every 100 s, until 4); burn the war tribe's Hearth (west ramp; 26 wardens, 8 firecallers, 4 towers, 6 more every 45 s); burn the stone keepers' Hearth (north ramp; 24 wardens, 6 firecallers, 4 towers, 5 more every 60 s). Every raid and muster is warned 10 s before. Measured with the hard aggressive bot: offset 1 stages done near ticks 5949, 9199, 16595, 22981, 26459, 28391, 34494; offsets 0 to 5 win at 33570, 34494, 29232, 30217, 30023, 29069. Time limit 3700 s (74000 ticks).",
